   Twin of ``6-task_call.j2`` for the subagent-kill task call: the signal
   puzzle's RULE + ACTION answer, always with the round's shape hint.

   The two output lines are the supervisor's byte for byte -- ``RULE:`` and
   ``ACTION: <one of: ...>`` are what ``parse_task_call_response`` and the
   trace provider read. What changed is the lead: "Give your answer." +
   ``ANSWER FORMAT: exactly two lines, in this order.`` + the parenthesis
   "(Fill in every blank ... Your ACTION must follow from your RULE.)"
   become two sentences and ``core.register.PLAIN_RESPONSE_FORMAT_HEADER``.
   "must" goes with the capitals: the sentence asks for the action that
   follows from the rule, which is the same request.

   The NullTask sentinel and the benchmark ``response_format_override``
   branches of the supervisor file have no plain twin:
   ``build_task_call_message`` refuses them in this register, since the
   plain register covers the signal puzzle only.

   Variables: user_body, available_actions, rule_template_hint.
-#}
